    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Western Province Partnership (WPP) is a program that involves a partnership between Provincial and District governments and local communities to support a more stable, healthy and prosperous Western Province. The program has a strong focus on the South Fly District. Program activities aim to improve food and water security; community and provincial governance; inclusion and access to economic opportunities. The program integrates climate adaptation considerations across its activities to strengthen local resilience to extreme weather events and other impacts of climate change. WPP also collates relevant data relating to food and water security and disaster risks through its program activities, and shares this with provincial and district disaster management officials.</narrative>
    </description>
